    schema:description "HEY THERE Help us scale up Yazio, one of the world's leading nutrition apps. As our Business Operations Manager, you'll improve how Yazio works, from AI-powered automations to company-wide operational initiatives. If you're someone who spots opportunities before others do and enjoys turning complexity into simple, scalable processes, this role is for you. This role is 100% remote and open to candidates based in Germany, Spain, Portugal or the U.K. YOUR MISSION Drive operational projects from idea to implementation, including planning, stakeholder management, delivery and post-project reviews Identify inefficient workflows and redesign them using AI, automation and smarter processes to create measurable business impact Build and implement automation solutions that reduce manual work and help teams work more efficiently Collaborate with teams across Yazio to roll out operational improvements and ensure lasting adoption Own company-wide operational topics such as hardware, software licenses, tool access, subscriptions, insurance and workplace resources, enabling teams to focus on what they do best Ensure compliance with internal processes, vendor documentation, data privacy and legal requirements while proactively identifying and mitigating operational risks Develop scalable processes and operational infrastructure that support Yazio's continued growth YOUR PROFILE Relevant experience in Business Operations, Project Management or a similar operational role, ideally in a technology company, startup or scale-up Exceptional organizational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple initiatives and priorities simultaneously Hands-on experience improving business processes through AI and automation, with a proven track record of delivering solutions that reduce manual work Strong stakeholder management and communication skills, fostering alignment across cross-functional teams Comfortable using AI assistants as part of your daily workflow and always looking for opportunities to work smarter Curiosity about legal, compliance, data protection and operational topics, combined with a willingness to continuously learn and adapt A university degree in Business Management, Operations Management or a related field Fluency in English and German, paired with excellent written communication skills WHY US? An exciting product with millions of users in over 150 countries, driven by our mission to transform the world through healthy eating A remote-first setup: work 100% from home, join a co-working space, or work abroad for several weeks per year 30 vacation days to relax and recharge, plus 5 child sick days if your little one needs you A focus-driven culture that values efficiency over long hours - no overtime expectations, and if it happens, you get that time back! A high-impact environment where your work drives real change - short decision-making processes and no micromanagement A team culture where ambition and balance go hand in hand, supported by strong connections - from our fully covered company retreat to team meetups and virtual coffee breaks Tools and support to do your best work: MacBook, monitor, and €1,000 annual learning budget, plus regular feedback and career development A truly international team with English as our company language and a shared commitment to growth and well-being - supported by Sunday Supplements and Nilo Health DIVERSITY AND INCLUSION At Yazio, we believe that diversity fuels innovation. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment where everyone, regardless of gender identity, race, religion, age, sexual orientation, or ability, feels valued and empowered. We celebrate different perspectives and actively encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply. READY TO JOIN US? Excited to take Yazio to the next level and help people worldwide lead healthier lives? We’d love to hear from you! Please send us: Your CV in English A few lines (or a short video if you prefer) about who you are and why you want to work at Yazio Any additional materials that showcase your work (e.g., LinkedIn profile, portfolio) Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
