    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "gtm-enablement-specialist-london-233491" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About 9fin 9fin is the AI platform powering global debt markets — the world’s largest asset class at over $145 trillion. Debt markets are vast, global, and mission-critical, yet still run on fragmented data, PDFs, and manual workflows. 9fin replaces this broken infrastructure with a single platform that centralises proprietary credit data, deep analysis, and high-value workflows across global markets. Today, 9fin powers teams at 300+ blue-chip institutions worldwide, including global banks, asset managers, private equity firms, law firms, and advisors. The business is scaling at exceptional speed, with rapid expansion in the US and best-in-class retention driven by deep workflow adoption. We’re at a defining inflection point. With proven product-market fit and strong, global market pull, 9fin is accelerating toward becoming the category-defining platform for debt markets worldwide. What you'll work on Every day is different, but here's an example of the kind of things you'll work on: Build 9fin's sales enablement function from the ground up, creating the playbooks, onboarding programs, and training frameworks that will scale our commercial team Design and deliver structured 30/60/90 day onboarding plans for SDRs, AEs, and sales leaders joining the UK team Run trainings on core sales methodologies (MEDDPICC, MEDDIC, BANT), the fundamentals of calling and email outreach, and deal strategy Partner closely with product to embed product knowledge into ongoing training, knowledge checks, and enablement content Develop persona-based training tailored to 9fin's customer segments — banks, asset managers, private equity firms, law firms, and advisors Sales tech stack training across Salesforce, HubSpot, Notion, Clay, Gong, Apollo, and our AI toolkit (Claude, ChatGPT, Granola) Document sales processes and lead change management as new programs, tools, and frameworks roll out across a fast-growing global team Build a career progression model and enablement pathway that supports growth across new business, account management, and customer success About You This role will be a great fit if you: Have direct sales experience, ideally as a former SDR manager looking to move into enablement, a closing AE, or someone already in a sales enablement role. You've carried a quota or coached a team that has, and salespeople respect you because of it Bring fintech or capital markets experience (or a strong track record in an adjacent, complex B2B space) Have hands-on experience building something from scratch — whether as a founding AE, an early SDR manager, or part of a team that stood up enablement in a scaling environment. You've written the playbook, not just delivered someone else's Are fluent with common sales methodologies (MEDDPICC, MEDDIC, BANT) and comfortable training reps and leaders on how to apply them Have strong AI fluency; you use Claude, ChatGPT, and Granola day-to-day, and you're the kind of person who builds skills, projects, and workflows to scale your own output Have led change management before; you can point to programs you've rolled out, obstacles you hit, and how you got the organization to adopt something new Cultivate strong relationships across the sales organization; because enablement is only effective when reps are genuinely bought in and want to engage Our Benefits We’re a scaling start up, and we enjoy sharing our success, when the company succeeds, we always reinvest that in our people. We also offer huge amounts of responsibility, an abundance of opportunity for growth and a platform to truly excel. Financial & Insurance Competitive Salary (our salary bands are benchmarked at the top end of the market) Equity Pension (your minimum contributions are 4% with 9fin matching up to 7%) Private Medical Insurance Paid sick leave with Income Protection for long periods of illness Group Life Assurance Season Ticket Loan & Cycle to Work schemes Time off 25 holiday days per year Local public holidays (with the ability to exchange them for alternative days) Hybrid working model, to allow you the flexibility to decide how, where and when you do your best work Work abroad for up to 3 months a year 1 month paid sabbatical after 5 years of service Enhanced parental leave & flexible working arrangements available Training & Culture Professional learning and development budget AI experimentation budget of £800 (UK) per employee to trial AI tools Bi-annual team socials Summer and Winter company social events 9fin is an equal opportunities employer At 9fin we are dedicated to building and promoting a fair and inclusive workplace where everyone can reach their full potential and truly belong. We recognize that building diverse teams enables a more creative and productive environment. If you’re excited about this role but your experience doesn’t perfectly align with the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You might just be who we’re looking for — either for this role, or perhaps another. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
