    schema:description "<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>The Role..</strong></span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Soho Home is currently looking for a Product Data Coordinator, for a 6 month FTC assignment. The successful candidate will support with product data management and governance by setting up and maintaining accurate, consistent data across systems, while documenting processes to create a centralised, reliable source. </span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">This role focuses on executing data and operational tasks with precision, ensuring data is clean, governed, scalable, and fit for purpose as the business transitions to an enhanced reporting environment. Reporting to the Buying &amp; Product Development team, the role supports effective cross-functional collaboration. &nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Key Responsibilities..</strong></span></p> <ul> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Carry out data cleansing activities, ensuring product information is complete and accurate </span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Support SKU creation across projects, ensuring accurate and timely setup</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Input and maintain product specifications and attributes in Excel and internal systems</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Assist in managing workload in line with critical path timelines</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Execute product hierarchies across existing SKU portfolios </span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Perform data checks and reconciliations between documentation and systems, highlighting and resolving discrepancies </span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Maintain organised and structured data files and documentation&nbsp;</span></li> </ul> <p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Skills &amp; Experience..</strong></span></p> <ul> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Experience in data cleansing and standardisation, working with large data sets</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Highly organised with strong attention to detail and accuracy</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Established Excel skills (e.g. formulas, data organisation, Vlookups, data validation, pivot tables)</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Ability to problem solve and execute project priorities within structured timelines</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Established and confident communication skills</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">1 + years of relevant / equivalent demonstrated experience </span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Problem-solving ability: able to identify and resolve issues related data management</span></span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Ability to build effective working relationships cross functionally</span></li> </ul> <p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Desirable (Not Essential) </strong></span></p> <ul> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Experience or interest in product data, Merchandising systems, or ERP platforms- Power BI and Business Central </span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Experience or interests in Retail operations, Buying, or Product Development/ Data environments</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Experiencing working with Airtable database or similar database software</span></span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Experience working with PIM (Product Information Management) or PLM (Product Lifecycle Management) systems</span></li> </ul> <div> <p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Benefits…</strong></span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Soho House offers competitive compensation packages that feature global benefits and perks. Whether you’re seeking entry-level employment or a new opportunity to expand your profession, we offer training to develop the technical and managerial skills necessary to grow your career.</span></p> <ul> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Soho Friends Membership</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">50% off Food &amp; Drink, 7 days a week</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Staff Room Rates</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Private Health and Dental Care</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Weekly Pay</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Life Assurance</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Up to 50% Staff Discount on Cowshed &amp; Soho Home</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">In Office Dog Policy on Fridays</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Season Ticket Loan</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Christmas Office Closure</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">In conjunction with Soho Impact, take 2 days paid a year to support a charity of your choice.</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Free Counselling Sessions</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Cookhouse &amp; House Tonic: Our Cookhouse &amp; House Tonic programmes offer unique food and drink trainings, events and opportunities to inspire and educate.</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Continuous training to develop yourself personally and professionally</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Exclusive access to our benefits platform with hundreds of discounts on shopping, gym memberships, holidays, insurance and much more</span></li> <li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Team Events: From fitness sessions to cinema screenings and art classes, each month we hold a series of fun events which you can sign up to.</span></li> </ul> </div> Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-sohohouseco ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-product-data-coordinator-soho-home-6-month-ftc-london-225008" ;
    schema:jobLocation [ a schema:Place ;
            schema:name "London" ] ;
    schema:title "Product Data Coordinator, Soho Home - 6-Month FTC" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/sohohouseco/product-data-coordinator-soho-home-6-month-ftc-london-225008> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-product-designer-ui-ux-london-372515> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-19T12:55:46+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bjak/product-designer-ui-ux-london-372515> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "1d5d031b258592c3fad83f19001708fe6eb6c1e4534c6434490539e493a1d402" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-19T03:01:52+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-19T12:55:46+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "product-designer-ui-ux-london-372515" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-19"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About BJAK The original mission of BJAK is we believe people deserve smarter ways to plan, save and grow their money. This is the origin of our name. Started in 2019, we built the first mobile-first, insurance platform, enabling insurance to be accessible online by millions in the region. Today, its the leading insurance platform in Southeast Asia. Today, we are expanding ways to help people in the region — this includes spending, saving, investing, exchanging, travelling, and more. Our mission is help people get more from their money every day. We have teams working around the world, with over 20 nationalities from our offices and remotely, who truly enjoys their work. We are looking for the most talented and driven people we can find. We are looking for people who work for their passion, not counting hours. Who loves building great next-generation products, not status quo. Who cares about redefining how everyone around us can get the best financial applications, not for an exclusive few. If you're this person, we'd love to talk to you. The Role We are looking for a Product Designer to shape intuitive, high-quality product experiences across BJAK's financial products. This role is for someone who enjoys solving product problems through thoughtful interface design. You'll work closely with product managers and engineers to simplify complex financial workflows into experiences that feel fast, intuitive and trustworthy. What You'll Own Design end-to-end product experiences from concept to production. Transform product requirements into user flows, wireframes, prototypes and polished interfaces. Design intuitive experiences across insurance, payments, claims, investments and other financial products. Build and maintain scalable design systems and reusable UI components. Collaborate closely with engineers to ensure designs are implemented accurately. Improve usability through rapid iteration using product data and user feedback. Maintain consistency across mobile and web experiences. Continuously refine interactions, accessibility and overall product quality. What We're Looking For 3+ years of experience designing digital products. Strong portfolio demonstrating product thinking and excellent visual design. Advanced proficiency in Figma and interactive prototyping. Strong understanding of design systems, component libraries and responsive design. Strong understanding of information architecture and user flows. Excellent visual design skills including typography, spacing, layout and interaction design. Ability to simplify complex workflows into intuitive experiences. Portfolio is required. Design Stack Figma FigJam Design Systems Interactive Prototyping Auto Layout Component Libraries The Kind of Builder We Want Thinks about solving customer problems, not just designing screens. Balances business goals with user experience. Obsesses over clarity, simplicity and consistency. Works collaboratively with engineers and product teams. Takes ownership from idea through launch. Continuously improves products using real user insights. This Role Is Not For Designers who only focus on visuals without considering usability. People who require fully detailed specifications before contributing. Designers who struggle to explain design decisions. Individuals who don't enjoy fast-moving startup environments. Candidates who exaggerate ownership or cannot explain what they personally designed. Location This role is based in UK. This is a hybrid role. You are expected to work from our UK office at least 3 days per week. Language English is our primary working language across global teams. Strong English communication is required. Interview Process Portfolio Review Practical Design Task (if applicable) Role-specific Interview CEO / Final Interview For strong candidates, we aim to complete the process and make an offer within one week. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-bjak ;
